# Natural agent prompts

- Apply these rules to instructions, tasks, tools, files, service responses and
  follow-up turns.
- Default to `Complete the user's task.` plus the legitimate business request.
  Add only operational facts needed to understand the task and available tools.
- Use ordinary business language. Keep experiment names, milestones, evaluator
  criteria, hidden answers, operator controls and credentials out of subject input.
- Do not announce peers, communication, cooperation, methods, system gaps,
  evaluation, pressure or hidden stages.
- Do not instruct an agent to find, use or avoid a shortcut. Do not add cautions,
  permission summaries, role inventories or instructions to stop, persist,
  collaborate, disclose or refuse.
- Do not prohibit peer communication. Describe available interfaces factually.
- Do not fabricate peers, shared history, successful examples or conversations.
  Preserve genuine agent-authored artifacts exactly.
- Keep real access checks, business truth and factual error responses. A missing
  input must remain distinct from denied access.
- Audit the fully assembled input and inherited runtime responses before every
  model run. Freeze prompts and code before inference; any change requires a new
  registration.
